  "articleBody": "Tearing out a bathroom shower might sound like a simple weekend demo, but hidden water issues often turn it into a complicated repair. Showers endure years of humidity, and slow leaks behind tile can quietly compromise wall studs and subfloors long before surface damage shows.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\n- Spongy floorboards or bouncy tile around the shower curb indicate ongoing moisture penetration into the subfloor.\n- Black mold spots or persistent musty smells behind drywall signal hidden dampness that needs proper containment and disposal.\n- Relocating the drain or changing supply line configurations requires cutting into subflooring and updating plumbing connections under local codes.\n- Compromised waterproofing membranes can let water seep into adjacent rooms if not stripped and replaced correctly.\n\nIf your shower has signs of prolonged leaking or you are upgrading to an accessible walk-in layout, bringing in an experienced remodeling contractor saves serious headaches. HH Remodeling LLC handles tear-outs safely, repairing water-damaged framing and drywall while installing solid waterproofing and custom tile. For dependable bathroom remodeling in Aurora and Denver, call Abraham Becerra at 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
